    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1552">

                <pb facs="0994" n="878" xml:id="pg878"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/71.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            French Chargé d’Affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1361.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of July 23d, with which you enclose a copy of a report,
                    dated July 15th, from the French Consular Agent at El Paso, Texas, covering the
                    treatment of the Christian Brothers of the Zacatecas School, at the hands of the
                    Constitutionalists.</p>
                <p>In reply you are informed that the Department has sent copies of this report to
                    its special representatives in Mexico, for their information in connection with
                    future representations they may be called upon to make in behalf of the
                    Christian Brothers.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
